-- title:
--   Additivity of ordDiff under scaling over a perfect field
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $F$ be fields with $F$ a $K$-algebra and $K$ perfect, and let $x \in F$ be an element such that $F$ is algebraic over the intermediate field $K(x) = K(\{x\})$ generated by $x$. Let $v$ be a place of $F$ over $K$ in the sense of this development: a valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $K$, different from all of $F$, and whose underlying ring is a principal ideal ring; write $\operatorname{ord}_v$ for the associated integer-valued order function, defined as minus the logarithm of the adic valuation attached to the height-one prime of $v$. Let $g \in F$ be nonzero and let $\omega \in \Omega_{F/K}$ be a nonzero Kähler differential. The quantity $\operatorname{ordDiff}_v(\omega)$ is by definition $\operatorname{ord}_v$ of the coefficient expressing $\omega$ as a multiple of $D_{K/F}(t)$, where $t$ is the chosen element of $F$ with $\operatorname{ord}_v(t) = 1$ (and the coefficient is taken to be $0$ if no such expression exists). The assertion is the equality of integers $$\operatorname{ordDiff}_v(g \cdot \omega) = \operatorname{ord}_v(g) + \operatorname{ordDiff}_v(\omega).$$
--
--   This is the expected behaviour of the order of a differential at a place under multiplication by a function, in the one-variable setting over a perfect base field: it is what makes the divisor of a nonzero differential well defined up to the divisor of a function. It is used in the computations of $\operatorname{ordDiff}$ of exact differentials $D(f)$ and of pullbacks of differentials along maps of function fields.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_Place_ordDiff_smul_of_perfectField.lean

